From: MX84 bring-up project
Subject: [PATCH] x86/boot: tolerate missing init_size from Cisco Miles

Cisco's old Miles payload clears boot_params and does not copy the
protocol-2.10 init_size field.  It does copy kernel_alignment.  This MX84
kernel uses a 16 MiB alignment which is larger than its initialization area,
so use that value when init_size is zero.

Without the fallback the decompressor places its page tables over the loaded
compressed kernel and resets before producing console output.

---
 arch/x86/boot/compressed/head_64.S | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/boot/compressed/head_64.S b/arch/x86/boot/compressed/head_64.S
--- a/arch/x86/boot/compressed/head_64.S
+++ b/arch/x86/boot/compressed/head_64.S
@@ -157,7 +157,13 @@ SYM_FUNC_START(startup_32)
 1:
 
 	/* Target address to relocate to for decompression */
-	addl	BP_init_size(%esi), %ebx
+	movl	BP_init_size(%esi), %eax
+	testl	%eax, %eax
+	jnz	.Lstartup32_have_init_size
+	/* Cisco Miles copies kernel_alignment but leaves init_size zero. */
+	movl	BP_kernel_alignment(%esi), %eax
+.Lstartup32_have_init_size:
+	addl	%eax, %ebx
 	subl	$ rva(_end), %ebx
 
 /*
-- 
2.43.0
